# tools/dpu_sigma_patch_test.py, Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), run 6, started 20261012T194600Z UTC.
# A mapping of REG_0 byte 0x7B (shift_bias << 2 | 1) over every shift_bias 0..63. Same method as runs 1-5
# (results/aie/dpu_sigma_patch_desktop2_20261012T182840Z.log, ..._20261012T191325Z.log,
# dpu_sigma_patch_bit7_desktop2_20261012T193618Z.log): the shift_cut-16 fixture compiled --fresh, the CACHED
# xmodel edited and reloaded without --fresh; idle check before each arm; the EP left every edited xmodel
# byte-identical and placed the Conv on the NPU in every arm. The tool now accepts shift_bias up to 63; its
# integer oracle caps the bias shift at 55 (int64), past which every model it scores reads the same.
# The run was wrapped in a keep-awake helper (SetThreadExecutionState for its lifetime only; lines below).
# Compiled xmodels and outputs stay in git-ignored scratch/.
#
# Pre-registration (sha256 64ef375113af8b2df26fef640c7afeef752101f63197a25355f1ecdb5fbe4c01):
#   written_utc 2026-10-12T19:45:46Z, before any run-6 arm has been loaded. A MAPPING run of REG_0 byte 0x7B (shift_bias << 2 | 1).
#   context: runs 3-5 (results/aie/dpu_sigma_patch_desktop2_20261012T191325Z.log, dpu_sigma_patch_bit7_desktop2_20261012T193618Z.log).
#     The shift_cut byte & 63 is the vsrs code (held on 19 held-out arms). The shift_bias field with bits 6-7 clear is in contract.
#     Bit 6 alone (shift_bias 16..31) acted as << (shift_bias & 15) on 5 informative arms. With bit 7 set, 0x81 kept an
#     unshifted bias, while 0x85, 0x91, 0xb1, 0xb9, 0xc1, 0xd1 read as no bias or a bias right-shifted by 4..8 or more.
#     "bit 7 zeroes the bias" was refuted by 0x81. The bits 6-7 behaviour is UNEXPLAINED.
#   test: tools/dpu_sigma_patch_test.py --site reg0 --base 16 --base-sb 0 --controls 15,1,16:15 --patches <grid6_arms.txt>
#     grid6_arms.txt (sha256 d6027d23fac886a29eb3f1af00962c7f62e433f63494235f658a1b615d5cc14a): every shift_bias 0..63 (bytes 0x01..0xfd) at shift_cut 1, plus at shift_cut
#     (shift_bias & 15) + 1 when that differs; 123 patched arms. At shift_cut 1, a bias down to ~b >> 8 shows; at (low + 1), a bias
#     of b << low sits mid-scale, so the two arms together bracket the effective bias.
#     Separation of the in-contract model from the alternatives per arm: prereg6_dry.txt (--dry-run --reference code6_sb4),
#     sha256 f08e1047e687d99f8ee56e615c6d00f3619f01b4e5914d160a63c98e392b0c49.
#     The run takes ~35 min, so it is wrapped in a keep-awake helper (SetThreadExecutionState for the run only).
#   decision rules: VOID if a control (15:0, 1:0, 16:15) is not EXACT. REJECTED if the EP rewrites the xmodel. A hang or
#     device error is recorded, and the remaining arms are not retried.
#   predictions:
#     P1 bits 6-7 clear, shift_bias 1..15 (30 arms, in contract): code6_sb4 matches every one.
#     P2 bit 6 only, shift_bias 16..31 (31 arms): code6_sb4 (bias << (shift_bias & 15)) matches every one.
#     P3 replication of run 5: 1:32 (0x81) matches code6_sb4 (unshifted bias); 1:48 (0xc1) matches code6_b7zero (no bias).
#     P4 bit 7 set (shift_bias 32..63, 62 arms minus the two in P3): NO prediction. This is the mapping. Each byte's effective
#        bias is reported post hoc by scratch fit_sb.py, extended to all shift_bias values, as a fit and not a result.
#        Any rule proposed from it needs its own held-out run.
